# Wrap-Up

<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;">

  <div>
    <h4 style="margin-top: 0; font-weight: bold;">In this professional learning module, you learned how to:</h4>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14pt">
      <li>Prepare to teach foundational data science concepts, including how data is collected, cleaned, visualized, and interpreted to generate insights.</li><br>
      <li>Support students in asking meaningful questions of data and using visualizations to tell clear, accurate, and responsible data stories.</li><br>
      <li>Guide students in reasoning about how AI systems use data, including limitations, bias, and the impact of data quality on outcomes.</li><br>
      <li>Prepare students for a culminating project by scaffolding data analysis, interpretation, and reflection on ethical and real-world implications of data and AI.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <img src="https://images.code.org/89644a0804bcdfc2839b17f70bcef23c-Screenshot 2025-12-04 at 2.33.30 PM.png" 
